, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "media.patriots.win", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATCIoMSbV.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://media.patriots.win/post/TifELyrBVkQY.jpeg", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [{"reference": "/scale/XmmTQn1X7ufIv2WY.png", "width": 353, "content-type": "png", "height": 768}], "blurhash": "U7Gbk:_N00D$~qIUWAxu008_~X%g00?bt8D%", "full_resolution": [2868, 1320]}, "title": "The Butt Baby", "last_comment_created": 1787083415744, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": true, "comments": 4, "score_up": 24, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "\ud83d\udca9\u00a0\u00a0POOPY\u00a0\u00a0DAYS", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATCIoLuht", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 35, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8786579, "raw_content": "This really is a state issue. It is easily remedied by local or state ordinances. \n\nWhen I was in high school, a local mosque installed loudspeakers and began to put out their daily call to prayer. When local government refused to follow local laws, adjacent churches quickly remedied this by installing loudspeakers and airing very loud Christian worship music simultaneously. This led to a bar (located near the mosque and churches) doing the same but with a local radio station. \n\nWithin a few weeks, the local government stepped in to stop everyone. \n\nIn most areas getting a straight ban against mosques doing these calls to prayer is virtually impossible. Politicians don't want to seem racist or bigoted but if you make it easy for them in this way, it's a much lower bar. ", "author": "DemPanicAtTheDisco", "created": 1787072799119, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "DemPanicAtTheDisco", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Proven strategy for banning loudspeaker Islamic calls to prayer at the state level", "last_comment_created": 1787075384053, "content": "<p>This really is a state issue. It is easily remedied by local or state ordinances.</p>\n<p>When I was in high school, a local mosque installed loudspeakers and began to put out their daily call to prayer. When local government refused to follow local laws, adjacent churches quickly remedied this by installing loudspeakers and airing very loud Christian worship music simultaneously. This led to a bar (located near the mosque and churches) doing the same but with a local radio station.</p>\n<p>Within a few weeks, the local government stepped in to stop everyone.</p>\n<p>In most areas getting a straight ban against mosques doing these calls to prayer is virtually impossible. Politicians don't want to seem racist or bigoted but if you make it easy for them in this way, it's a much lower bar.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 5, "score_up": 35, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "2089712160981090681", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATCIoLuNE", "is_twitter": true, "is_admin": false, "score": 37, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8786528, "raw_content": "", "author": "PiratePatriotParrot", "creat